      "params": [],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Reset the history of the value returned by GetAverageRequiredTexturePoolSize()"
    },
    {
      "id": "get-average-required-texture-pool-size",
      "name": "GetAverageRequiredTexturePoolSize",
      "category": "TextureStreamingTypes",
      "signature": "GetAverageRequiredTexturePoolSize()",
      "params": [],
      "returnType": "Int64",
      "docs": "Returns the average value of the required texture pool \"r.streaming.PoolSize\" since engine start or since the last ResetAverageRequiredTexturePoolSize().\nThis value gives the perfect value for \"r.streaming.PoolSize\" so that the streamer would always have enough memory to stream in everything.\nThe requirements are different depending on whether GPoolSizeVRAMPercentage > 0 or not.\nWhen GPoolSizeVRAMPercentage > 0, the non streaming mips are not accounted in the required pool size since StreamingPool = Min(TexturePool, GPoolSizeVRAMPercentage * VRAM - RenderTargets - NonStreamingTexture)\nThis means that the StreamingPool = TexturePool, unless there is not enough VRAM\nOtherwise, when GPoolSizeVRAMPercentage == 0, StreamingPool = TexturePool - NonStreamingTexture. In which case \"r.streaming.PoolSize\" must account for the size of NonStreamingTexture"
    }
  ]
